# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MyNest Design Studio — Frontend environment (EXAMPLE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust values as needed:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# SECURITY NOTE:
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with `VITE_`, and every one of
# them is bundled into the PUBLIC client code shipped to browsers.
# NEVER put secrets or API keys in this file — anything here is visible
# to end users. All secrets (including AI provider keys) live ONLY in
# the backend .env.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# API base URL.
# In development the Vite dev server proxies `/api/*` to the backend
# (see vite.config.ts), so this can stay blank locally.
# For production builds (no dev proxy), set this to the deployed API
# origin, e.g. https://api.mynest.example.com
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# ── Planned / future values (leave commented until implemented) ──
# Public feature flags (safe to expose to the browser):
# VITE_ENABLE_AI_STUDIO=false

# Client-side error monitoring — public DSN only, never a secret key:
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
